{"availability":"available","full":"estrelajs/estrela","name":"estrela","description":"Full Reactive Framework.","category":"Developer tools","language":"TypeScript","stars":51,"forks":0,"created":"2022-03-01T15:05:06Z","updated":"2024-06-18T20:39:31Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://estrelajs.github.io/","topics":["framework","reactive","webapp"],"demo":"https://estrelajs.github.io/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T13:01:32.437Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T13:01:32.437Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T13:01:32.437Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T13:01:32.437Z","stars":51,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Estrela is a Javascript framework to develop reactive web apps.","Estrela is a modern TypeScript library inspired by popular frameworks such as React, Angular, and Solid. It provides a comprehensive set of features while leveraging reactive programming to create responsive and dynamic applications."],"features":["Reactive Signal-based Framework: Estrela's core architecture is built around signals, enabling reactive programming. Signals allow for efficient data flow and automatically update the UI whenever the underlying data…","Main Functionalities: Estrela comes with all the essential functionalities you need to build robust applications. It provides components, lifecycle hooks, and utilities for managing state, handling events, and rendering…","Built-in Styling with CSS-in-JS: Estrela incorporates CSS-in-JS styling, allowing you to write component-specific styles directly in your TypeScript code. This approach promotes component encapsulation and eliminates…","Router: The built-in router simplifies navigation within your application. It provides declarative routing capabilities, enabling you to define routes and associated components effortlessly.","Store: Estrela includes a powerful store mechanism for managing global state. The store facilitates state sharing acr